##
Results that never arrive, and nothing used as though it were something.

This program does not compile. A function that says it yields a value must reach one on
every path, and a call that yields nothing has no result to pass anywhere — not even to
Console.WriteLine, which takes a value of any kind but still takes a value.
##

global model Program

    # This says it yields a string and never yields at all.
    string function Describe()
        Console.WriteLine("describing");
    end function

    # This yields one only when the score is high enough.
    string function Grade(integer score)
        if score >= 60
            yield "pass";
        end if
    end function

    # Insert changes the set in place and yields nothing, so there is nothing to write.
    function Main()
        integer[] scores = {90, 72};

        Console.WriteLine(scores.InsertAt(1, 80));

        # Nor to pass on, however willing the parameter.
        Console.Write(Program.Shout());
    end function

    function Shout()
        Console.WriteLine("oi");
    end function

end model
